• Editing of country and thematic files, mainly in the area of ​​the EU's Common Foreign and Security Policy (CFSP) and on Switzerland-EU relations in general;
• Coordination and creation of visit dossiers; Participation in the preparation of political consultations;
• Creation of information tables for the foreign policy commissions of the National Council and the Council of States;
• If necessary, support other sections within the EU coordination in other policy areas.
• University degree (Master);
• strong interest in Swiss European policy;
• independent and efficient way of working, ability to work precisely and accurately, organizational talent, sociable and enthusiastic, flexible and resilient;
• very good editorial skills; You find it easy to reduce complex issues to the essentials and formulate them in a way that is tailored to the target group;
• Willingness to delve into thematically different dossiers depending on the needs of the department;
• Very good oral and written knowledge of two official languages ​​as well as English.

